  "question": {
    "text": "In the given circuits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced></math>, switches&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">S</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">S</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are closed at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;kept close for a long time. The variation of currents in the two circuits for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mtext><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;shown in the options.&nbsp;(Figures are schematic and not drawn to scale.)<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7ffa1d61-53d0-417e-9169-ec7910377604-D716.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 143px;\" />",
